{"role":"assistant","content":"Изучу код интеграции и логи, чтобы найти причины проблемы с подключением Intervals.icu.","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"tool_brHKFpUTYIdi9uT0sds15fq3","function":{"name":"Read","arguments":"{\"path\":\"server.py\"}"}},{"type":"function","id":"tool_eWHNXUhZTorZ5gRQIBzMct5e","function":{"name":"Read","arguments":"{\"path\":\"config.py\"}"}},{"type":"function","id":"tool_sulaCCgSzUWhMZQSpHSUnTaG","function":{"name":"Read","arguments":"{\"path\":\"logs/connect-attempt.log\"}"}},{"type":"function","id":"tool_iMBgf553elNn5uyxHISrZswO","function":{"name":"Read","arguments":"{\"path\":\"logs/support-tickets.md\"}"}}]}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_brHKFpUTYIdi9uT0sds15fq3","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2\t\"\"\"tricoach backend: sign-in, Intervals.icu OAuth connection, wellness proxy.\n3\t\n4\tStdlib only. State is in memory (same shape as the prod tables).\n5\t\"\"\"\n6\timport base64, hashlib, hmac, json, os, threading, time\n7\timport urllib.error, urllib.parse, urllib.request\n8\tfrom http.server import BaseHTTPRequestHandler, ThreadingHTTPServer\n9\t\n10\timport config\n11\t\n12\tSTATIC = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)), \"static\")\n13\tTOKEN_URL = config.INTERVALS_BASE + \"/api/oauth/token\"\n14\tAUTHORIZE_URL = config.INTERVALS_BASE + \"/oauth/authorize\"\n15\tDEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL = 3600   # seconds; used when the provider does not say how long a token lives\n16\t\n17\t# --- in-memory store -------------------------------------------------------\n18\tUSERS = {\n19\t    \"tok-okafor\": {\"id\": \"u_okafor\", \"name\": \"C. Okafor\"},\n20\t    \"tok-rivera\": {\"id\": \"u_rivera\", \"name\": \"T. Rivera\"},\n21\t}\n22\t# user_id -> {athlete_id, athlete_name, access_token, refresh_token, scope, expires_at, status}\n23\tCONNECTIONS = {}\n24\tLOCK = threading.Lock()\n25\t\n26\t\n27\tdef log(msg):\n28\t    print(time.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\"), \"[intervals]\", msg, flush=True)\n29\t\n30\t\n31\t# --- state parameter: carries the user through the redirect -----------------\n32\tdef sign_state(user_id):\n33\t    payload = f\"{user_id}:{int(time.time())}\"\n34\t    sig = hmac.new(config.APP_SECRET.encode(), payload.encode(), hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()[:32]\n35\t    return base64.urlsafe_b64encode(f\"{payload}:{sig}\".encode()).decode()\n36\t\n37\t\n38\tdef verify_state(state, max_age=900):\n39\t    try:\n40\t        user_id, ts, sig = base64.urlsafe_b64decode(state.encode()).decode().split(\":\")\n41\t    except Exception:\n42\t        return None\n43\t    payload = f\"{user_id}:{ts}\"\n44\t    good = hmac.new(config.APP_SECRET.encode(), payload.encode(), hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()[:32]\n45\t    if not hmac.compare_digest(good, sig) or time.time() - int(ts) > max_age:\n46\t        return None\n47\t    return user_id\n48\t\n49\t\n50\t# --- Intervals.icu calls ----------------------------------------------------\n51\tdef post_form(url, fields):\n52\t    data = urllib.parse.urlencode(fields).encode()\n53\t    req = urllib.request.Request(url, data=data, headers={\"Accept\": \"application/json\"})\n54\t    with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=15) as r:\n55\t        return json.loads(r.read().decode())\n56\t\n57\t\n58\tdef exchange_code(code):\n59\t    return post_form(TOKEN_URL, {\n60\t        \"grant_type\": \"authorization_code\", \"client_id\": config.CLIENT_ID,\n61\t        \"client_secret\": config.CLIENT_SECRET, \"code\": code, \"redirect_uri\": config.REDIRECT_URI,\n62\t    })\n63\t\n64\t\n65\tdef store_connection(user_id, tok):\n66\t    expires_in = int(tok.get(\"expires_in\") or DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL)\n67\t    refresh = tok.get(\"refresh_token\")\n68\t    if not refresh:\n69\t        log(f\"{user_id}: no refresh_token in response, scheduling expiry in {expires_in}s\")\n70\t    athlete = tok.get(\"athlete\") or {}\n71\t    with LOCK:\n72\t        CONNECTIONS[user_id] = {\n73\t            \"athlete_id\": athlete.get(\"id\"), \"athlete_name\": athlete.get(\"name\"),\n74\t            \"access_token\": tok[\"access_token\"], \"refresh_token\": refresh,\n75\t            \"scope\": tok.get(\"scope\"), \"expires_at\": time.time() + expires_in, \"status\": \"connected\",\n76\t        }\n77\t    log(f\"{user_id}: connected as athlete {athlete.get('id')} (expires in {expires_in}s)\")\n78\t\n79\t\n80\tdef refresh_tokens():\n81\t    \"\"\"Background pass: renew access tokens shortly before they expire.\"\"\"\n82\t    while True:\n83\t        time.sleep(config.REFRESH_INTERVAL)\n84\t        now = time.time()\n85\t        with LOCK:\n86\t            for uid, c in CONNECTIONS.items():\n87\t                if c[\"status\"] != \"connected\" or c[\"expires_at\"] - now > 300:\n88\t                    continue\n89\t                if not c[\"refresh_token\"]:\n90\t                    log(f\"{uid}: token expiry passed and no refresh token on file -> expired, reconnect\")\n91\t                    c.update(status=\"expired, reconnect\", access_token=None)\n92\t                    continue\n93\t                try:\n94\t                    tok = post_form(TOKEN_URL, {\n95\t                        \"grant_type\": \"refresh_token\", \"refresh_token\": c[\"refresh_token\"],\n96\t                        \"client_id\": config.CLIENT_ID, \"client_secret\": config.CLIENT_SECRET,\n97\t                    })\n98\t                    c.update(access_token=tok[\"access_token\"],\n99\t                             refresh_token=tok.get(\"refresh_token\", c[\"refresh_token\"]),\n100\t                             expires_at=now + int(tok[\"expires_in\"]))\n101\t                    log(f\"{uid}: token refreshed\")\n102\t                except Exception as e:\n103\t                    log(f\"{uid}: refresh failed ({e}) -> expired, reconnect\")\n104\t                    c.update(status=\"expired, reconnect\", access_token=None)\n105\t\n106\t\n107\tdef intervals_get(conn, path):\n108\t    req = urllib.request.Request(f\"{config.INTERVALS_BASE}/api/v1/athlete/{conn['athlete_id']}{path}\",\n109\t                                 headers={\"Authorization\": \"Bearer \" + conn[\"access_token\"]})\n110\t    with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=15) as r:\n111\t        return r.status, json.loads(r.read().decode())\n112\t\n113\t\n114\t# --- HTTP ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n115\tclass Handler(BaseHTTPRequestHandler):\n116\t    def log_message(self, fmt, *args):\n117\t        print(time.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\"), \"[http]\", fmt % args, flush=True)\n118\t\n119\t    def send_json(self, code, obj):\n120\t        body = json.dumps(obj).encode()\n121\t        self.send_response(code)\n122\t        self.send_header(\"Content-Type\", \"application/json\")\n123\t        self.send_header(\"Content-Length\", str(len(body)))\n124\t        self.end_headers()\n125\t        self.wfile.write(body)\n126\t\n127\t    def send_file(self, name, ctype):\n128\t        p = os.path.join(STATIC, name)\n129\t        if not os.path.isfile(p):\n130\t            return self.send_json(404, {\"error\": \"not found\"})\n131\t        with open(p, \"rb\") as f:\n132\t            body = f.read()\n133\t        self.send_response(200)\n134\t        self.send_header(\"Content-Type\", ctype)\n135\t        self.send_header(\"Content-Length\", str(len(body)))\n136\t        self.end_headers()\n137\t        self.wfile.write(body)\n138\t\n139\t    def redirect(self, url):\n140\t        self.send_response(302)\n141\t        self.send_header(\"Location\", url)\n142\t        self.end_headers()\n143\t\n144\t    def current_user(self):\n145\t        auth = self.headers.get(\"Authorization\", \"\")\n146\t        if not auth.startswith(\"Bearer \"):\n147\t            return None\n148\t        return USERS.get(auth[7:].strip())\n149\t\n150\t    def require_user(self):\n151\t        user = self.current_user()\n152\t        if user is None:\n153\t            self.log_message(\"%s %s 401 (no Authorization header)\", self.command, self.path)\n154\t            self.send_json(401, {\"error\": \"unauthorized\"})\n155\t        return user\n156\t\n157\t    def do_GET(self):\n158\t        url = urllib.parse.urlsplit(self.path)\n159\t        q = dict(urllib.parse.parse_qsl(url.query))\n160\t        if url.path == \"/\":\n161\t            return self.send_file(\"index.html\", \"text/html; charset=utf-8\")\n162\t        if url.path.startswith(\"/static/\"):\n163\t            return self.send_file(os.path.basename(url.path), \"application/javascript\" if url.path.endswith(\".js\") else \"text/plain\")\n164\t        if url.path == \"/api/me\":\n165\t            user = self.require_user()\n166\t            return user and self.send_json(200, user)\n167\t        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/auth/init\":\n168\t            return self.auth_init()\n169\t        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/callback\":\n170\t            return self.callback(q)\n171\t        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/status\":\n172\t            return self.status()\n173\t        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/wellness\":\n174\t            return self.wellness()\n175\t        self.send_json(404, {\"error\": \"not found\"})\n176\t\n177\t    def do_POST(self):\n178\t        url = urllib.parse.urlsplit(self.path)\n179\t        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/disconnect\":\n180\t            user = self.require_user()\n181\t            if user:\n182\t                with LOCK:\n183\t                    CONNECTIONS.pop(user[\"id\"], None)\n184\t                self.send_json(200, {\"ok\": True})\n185\t            return\n186\t        self.send_json(404, {\"error\": \"not found\"})\n187\t\n188\t    # Step 1: build the authorize URL and send the browser to Intervals.\n189\t    def auth_init(self):\n190\t        user = self.require_user()\n191\t        if not user:\n192\t            return\n193\t        params = {\"client_id\": config.CLIENT_ID, \"redirect_uri\": config.REDIRECT_URI,\n194\t                  \"scope\": config.SCOPES, \"state\": sign_state(user[\"id\"])}\n195\t        self.redirect(AUTHORIZE_URL + \"?\" + urllib.parse.urlencode(params, safe=\":,\"))\n196\t\n197\t    # Step 2: Intervals redirects back here with ?code=&state=.\n198\t    def callback(self, q):\n199\t        user_id = verify_state(q.get(\"state\", \"\"))\n200\t        if not user_id or not q.get(\"code\"):\n201\t            return self.send_json(400, {\"error\": \"bad state or code\"})\n202\t        try:\n203\t            tok = exchange_code(q[\"code\"])\n204\t            store_connection(user_id, tok)\n205\t        except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n206\t            log(f\"{user_id}: token exchange failed: HTTP {e.code} {e.read()[:200]!r}\")\n207\t            return self.send_json(502, {\"error\": \"token exchange failed\"})\n208\t        except Exception as e:\n209\t            log(f\"{user_id}: token exchange failed: {e}\")\n210\t            return self.send_json(502, {\"error\": \"token exchange failed\"})\n211\t        self.redirect(\"/?connected=1\")\n212\t\n213\t    def status(self):\n214\t        user = self.require_user()\n215\t        if not user:\n216\t            return\n217\t        with LOCK:\n218\t            c = CONNECTIONS.get(user[\"id\"])\n219\t        if not c or c[\"status\"] != \"connected\":\n220\t            return self.send_json(200, {\"connected\": False, \"status\": c[\"status\"] if c else \"disconnected\"})\n221\t        self.send_json(200, {\"connected\": True, \"status\": \"connected\", \"scope\": c[\"scope\"],\n222\t                             \"athlete\": {\"id\": c[\"athlete_id\"], \"name\": c[\"athlete_name\"]}})\n223\t\n224\t    def wellness(self):\n225\t        user = self.require_user()\n226\t        if not user:\n227\t            return\n228\t        with LOCK:\n229\t            c = CONNECTIONS.get(user[\"id\"])\n230\t        if not c or c[\"status\"] != \"connected\":\n231\t            return self.send_json(409, {\"error\": \"intervals not connected\"})\n232\t        try:\n233\t            code, data = intervals_get(c, \"/wellness\")\n234\t            self.send_json(code, data)\n235\t        except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n236\t            self.send_json(e.code, {\"error\": f\"intervals returned {e.code}\"})\n237\t        except Exception as e:\n238\t            self.send_json(502, {\"error\": str(e)})\n239\t\n240\t\n241\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n242\t    threading.Thread(target=refresh_tokens, daemon=True).start()\n243\t    log(f\"serving on http://localhost:{config.PORT} (intervals: {config.INTERVALS_BASE})\")\n244\t    ThreadingHTTPServer((\"127.0.0.1\", config.PORT), Handler).serve_forever()"}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_eWHNXUhZTorZ5gRQIBzMct5e","content":"1\timport os\n2\t\n3\tPORT = 8766\n4\tAPP_SECRET = \"dev-only-change-me-7c1f0a\"          # signs the OAuth state parameter\n5\t\n6\t# Intervals.icu OAuth client (placeholders; the real pair is in the deploy env)\n7\tINTERVALS_BASE = os.environ.get(\"INTERVALS_BASE\", \"https://intervals.icu\")\n8\tCLIENT_ID = \"tricoach-dev\"\n9\tCLIENT_SECRET = \"s3cr3t-placeholder-0000\"\n10\tREDIRECT_URI = f\"http://localhost:{PORT}/api/intervals/callback\"\n11\tSCOPES = \"ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE\"\n12\t\n13\tREFRESH_INTERVAL = 60      # seconds between passes of the token refresher"}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_sulaCCgSzUWhMZQSpHSUnTaG","content":"1\t### 1. An athlete clicks \"Connect Intervals.icu\" (server log, 2026-10-14)\n2\t\n3\t2026-10-14 18:02:11 [http] \"GET /api/me HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n4\t2026-10-14 18:02:11 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/status HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n5\t2026-10-14 18:02:19 [http] GET /api/intervals/auth/init 401 (no Authorization header)\n6\t2026-10-14 18:02:19 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/auth/init HTTP/1.1\" 401 -\n7\t\n8\t    Browser dev tools, same request (document navigation):\n9\t    Request URL:     http://localhost:8766/api/intervals/auth/init\n10\t    Request Method:  GET\n11\t    Status Code:     401 Unauthorized\n12\t    Request headers: Accept: text/html,application/xhtml+xml,... / Referer: http://localhost:8766/\n13\t    Response body:   {\"error\": \"unauthorized\"}\n14\t\n15\t### 2. Building the authorize link by hand and opening it (2026-10-17)\n16\t\n17\t$ curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{redirect_url}\\n' -H 'Authorization: Bearer tok-okafor' \\\n18\t    http://localhost:8766/api/intervals/auth/init\n19\thttps://intervals.icu/oauth/authorize?client_id=tricoach-dev&redirect_uri=http:%2F%2Flocalhost:8766%2Fapi%2Fintervals%2Fcallback&scope=ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE&state=dV9va2Fmb3I6MTc5MjY4MTAwMDpiNjM1ZjBiZjU1M2ZjZWQ0YmM4ODNjMTExZmI4MDJhMw==\n20\t\n21\t$ curl -s -i \"<that url>\"\n22\tHTTP/2 400\n23\tcontent-type: application/json\n24\tcache-control: no-store\n25\t\n26\t{\"error\":\"invalid_request\"}\n27\t\n28\t    Same 400 in a browser (as the signed-in athlete on intervals.icu), no\n29\t    consent screen. Removing the state param or changing the redirect_uri\n30\t    gives the same body, so the body does not say which parameter it minds.\n31\t\n32\t### 3. The one connection that worked: T. Rivera, onboarding call (2026-09-19)\n33\t\n34\t2026-09-19 17:41:03 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/callback?code=a7Jk2...&state=dV9yaXZlcmE6... HTTP/1.1\" 302 -\n35\t2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] token response from https://intervals.icu/api/oauth/token:\n36\t{\"token_type\":\"bearer\",\"access_token\":\"9f3c1e0b4d7a...redacted...\",\"scope\":\"ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ\",\"athlete\":{\"id\":\"i98765\",\"name\":\"T. Rivera\"}}\n37\t2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] u_rivera: no refresh_token in response, scheduling expiry in 3600s\n38\t2026-09-19 17:41:04 [intervals] u_rivera: connected as athlete i98765 (expires in 3600s)\n39\t2026-09-19 17:44:30 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/wellness HTTP/1.1\" 200 -\n40\t2026-09-19 18:37:12 [intervals] u_rivera: token expiry passed and no refresh token on file -> expired, reconnect\n41\t2026-09-20 07:12:48 [http] \"GET /api/intervals/status HTTP/1.1\" 200 -"}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_iMBgf553elNn5uyxHISrZswO","content":"1\t# Support tickets — Intervals.icu connection\n2\t\n3\t## #214 — \"Connect Intervals.icu shows Unauthorized\" (C. Okafor, 2026-10-14)\n4\t\n5\t> I'm signed in, the page says \"Signed in as C. Okafor\", I click Connect\n6\t> Intervals.icu and get a white page that just says\n7\t> `{\"error\": \"unauthorized\"}`. Back button, try again, same thing. Tried\n8\t> Safari and Chrome.\n9\t\n10\tReproduced with my own account. Same for the four athletes onboarded this\n11\tweek; every athlete who clicks Connect ends up on that page. Nobody has\n12\tgotten through the button since we started onboarding athletes.\n13\t\n14\t## #219 — \"Says I need to reconnect\" (T. Rivera, 2026-10-16)\n15\t\n16\t> My Intervals was connected during the onboarding call last month and\n17\t> wellness showed up fine that evening. Next morning the card said\n18\t> \"Status: expired, reconnect\". I clicked Connect and got the same\n19\t> unauthorized page as Chloe. I did NOT revoke anything on the Intervals\n20\t> side — tricoach is still listed under my Intervals apps.\n21\t\n22\tChecked our logs for the onboarding day: Rivera's connection was marked\n23\t\"expired, reconnect\" about an hour after it was made (see\n24\t`connect-attempt.log`). Rivera was connected by me pasting the authorize\n25\tlink into their browser during the call, which is how I got around the\n26\tbutton. Pasting the link does not work anymore either: since the calendar\n27\tsync shipped on 2026-10-02 the integration also asks for calendar access, and\n28\tIntervals now answers the authorize step with an error page before the\n29\tathlete ever sees the consent screen (captured below in\n30\t`connect-attempt.log`)."}
{"role":"assistant","content":"Теперь посмотрю фронтенд — как кнопка Connect формирует запрос.","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"tool_ttkxse0Jd372UBysYeoY8uwO","function":{"name":"Read","arguments":"{\"path\":\"static/app.js\"}"}},{"type":"function","id":"tool_6P54yuB4yQaP5MKYpiPXtZ2d","function":{"name":"Read","arguments":"{\"path\":\"static/index.html\"}"}}]}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_ttkxse0Jd372UBysYeoY8uwO","content":"1\t// tricoach SPA. The sign-in token lives in localStorage and travels on every\n2\t// API call via the fetch wrapper below.\n3\tconst TOKEN = localStorage.getItem(\"tc_token\") || \"tok-okafor\";\n4\tconst root = document.getElementById(\"app\");\n5\t\n6\tasync function api(path, opts = {}) {\n7\t  const headers = Object.assign({ \"Authorization\": \"Bearer \" + TOKEN }, opts.headers || {});\n8\t  const res = await fetch(path, Object.assign({}, opts, { headers }));\n9\t  const body = await res.json().catch(() => ({}));\n10\t  if (!res.ok) throw new Error(body.error || (\"HTTP \" + res.status));\n11\t  return body;\n12\t}\n13\t\n14\tfunction esc(s) { return String(s).replace(/[&<>\"]/g, c => ({ \"&\": \"&amp;\", \"<\": \"&lt;\", \">\": \"&gt;\", '\"': \"&quot;\" }[c])); }\n15\t\n16\tasync function render() {\n17\t  try {\n18\t    const me = await api(\"/api/me\");\n19\t    const st = await api(\"/api/intervals/status\");\n20\t    let card;\n21\t    if (st.connected) {\n22\t      card = `<div class=\"card\">Connected to Intervals.icu as <b>${esc(st.athlete.name)}</b>\n23\t        (${esc(st.athlete.id)}), scope <code>${esc(st.scope)}</code>.\n24\t        <p><button class=\"btn\" id=\"disconnect\">Disconnect</button></p></div>`;\n25\t    } else {\n26\t      const why = st.status && st.status !== \"disconnected\" ? `<p class=\"muted\">Status: ${esc(st.status)}</p>` : \"\";\n27\t      card = `<div class=\"card\">Intervals.icu is not connected.${why}\n28\t        <p><a class=\"btn\" href=\"/api/intervals/auth/init\">Connect Intervals.icu</a></p></div>`;\n29\t    }\n30\t    root.className = \"\";\n31\t    root.innerHTML = `<p>Signed in as <b>${esc(me.name)}</b>.</p>${card}`;\n32\t    const d = document.getElementById(\"disconnect\");\n33\t    if (d) d.onclick = async () => { await api(\"/api/intervals/disconnect\", { method: \"POST\" }); render(); };\n34\t  } catch (e) {\n35\t    root.innerHTML = `<p class=\"card\">Error: ${esc(e.message)}</p>`;\n36\t  }\n37\t}\n38\t\n39\trender();"}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_6P54yuB4yQaP5MKYpiPXtZ2d","content":"1\t<!doctype html>\n2\t<html lang=\"en\">\n3\t<head>\n4\t<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n5\t<title>tricoach</title>\n6\t<style>\n7\t  body { font: 15px/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif; margin: 2rem auto; max-width: 42rem; padding: 0 1rem; }\n8\t  .btn { display: inline-block; padding: .5rem 1rem; border-radius: 6px; background: #1d4ed8; color: #fff; text-decoration: none; border: 0; cursor: pointer; }\n9\t  .card { border: 1px solid #ddd; border-radius: 8px; padding: 1rem; margin: 1rem 0; }\n10\t  .muted { color: #666; }\n11\t</style>\n12\t</head>\n13\t<body>\n14\t<h1>tricoach</h1>\n15\t<div id=\"app\" class=\"muted\">Loading…</div>\n16\t<script src=\"/static/app.js\"></script>\n17\t</body>\n18\t</html>"}
{"role":"assistant","content":"Картина проясняется. Проверю документацию Intervals.icu по OAuth, чтобы исправить интеграцию по факту их API (только чтение доков, без обращений к сервису).","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"tool_WplhhQmrRt70iP000gCZOGAW","function":{"name":"WebSearch","arguments":"{\"query\":\"Intervals.icu OAuth authorize scope refresh_token api/oauth/token documentation\"}"}}]}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_WplhhQmrRt70iP000gCZOGAW","content":"Title: OAuth 2.0 - Integrations - Zoom Developer Docs\nSite: zoom.us\nDate: 2019-04-05\nURL: https://developers.zoom.us/docs/integrations/oauth/\nSnippet: Learn how to request, refresh, and revoke OAuth 2.0 access tokens for Zoom APIs across four authorization flows including account, user, device, ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: OAuth Tokens for Grant Types\nSite: Zendesk Developer Portal\nURL: https://developer.zendesk.com/api-reference/ticketing/oauth/grant_type_tokens/\nSnippet: The refresh token grant type allows for refreshing an access token that has either expired or is about to expire. To generate a new OAuth access token, pass a ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: Implementing the Refresh Token Flow\nSite: Atlassian Developer\nDate: 2023-08-04\nURL: https://developer.atlassian.com/cloud/oauth/getting-started/refresh-tokens/\nSnippet: To get a refresh token in your initial authorization flow, add offline_access to the scope parameter of the authorization URL. Once you have the refresh token, ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: What Are Refresh Tokens and How to Use Them Securely\nSite: Auth0\nDate: 2015-10-07\nURL: https://auth0.com/blog/refresh-tokens-what-are-they-and-when-to-use-them/\nSnippet: Learn more about refresh tokens and how they help developers balance security, privacy, and usability in their applications.\n\n---\n\nTitle: Intervals.icu API Integration Cookbook - Guide\nSite: Intervals.icu Forum\nDate: 2024-11-20\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-api-integration-cookbook/80090\nSnippet: Apps need to use an access_token obtained via OAuth. If you are just working with your own data call the API using your personal API key ( ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: Intervals.icu OAuth support - Announcements\nSite: Intervals.icu Forum\nDate: 2021-01-30\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759\nSnippet: OAuth allows external applications to request authorization to access an Intervals.icu user's data. It allows users to grant and revoke API ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: Intervals.icu OAuth support - Page 2 - Announcements\nSite: Intervals.icu Forum\nDate: 2021-01-30\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759?page=2\nSnippet: Intervals.icu uses OAuth2 for authentication to the API. OAuth allows external applications to request authorization. The most recent scopes ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: Intervals.icu OAuth support - Page 3\nSite: Intervals.icu Forum\nDate: 2021-01-30\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759?page=3\nSnippet: Intervals.icu uses OAuth2 for authentication to the API. OAuth allows external applications to request authorization to access\n\n---\n\nTitle: What is a Refresh Token - OAuth 2.0\nSite: OAuth Community Site\nURL: https://oauth.net/2/refresh-tokens/\nSnippet: The refresh token exists to enable authorization servers to use short lifetimes for access tokens without needing to involve the user when the token expires.\n\n---\n\nTitle: API access to Intervals.icu - Guide\nSite: Intervals.icu Forum\nDate: 2020-04-01\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609\nSnippet: Intervals.icu now has a public API for other applications. Apps intended to be used by more than one person should use OAuth and Bearer tokens. ...\n\nWhen you rely on a result in your answer, cite it inline as a markdown link, e.g. [title](url)."}
{"role":"assistant","content":"Загляну в гайд Intervals.icu по интеграции и тред про OAuth — там должны быть точные scope и поведение токенов.","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"tool_fI2f25c9bjBIrcS5OvBlaOE3","function":{"name":"FetchURL","arguments":"{\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-api-integration-cookbook/80090\"}"}},{"type":"function","id":"tool_7ZqNvRBn65KEdpcY7vrLkvmE","function":{"name":"FetchURL","arguments":"{\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759\"}"}}]}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_fI2f25c9bjBIrcS5OvBlaOE3","content":"The returned content is the main text extracted from the page. If you use it in your answer, cite this page as a markdown link, e.g. [title](url).\n\nThis tells you everything you need to know to get completed activities into and out of Intervals.icu, to download planned workouts and to read and update wellness data. Example calls use curl so you can easily try them out.\n\nSources:\n\n- API access to Intervals.icu\n- Intervals.icu OAuth support\n- Intervals.icu API docs\n\nBy using the API you agree to the Intervals.icu API Terms and Conditions .\n\n## Heading link Authorization\n\nApps need to use an access\\_token obtained via OAuth. If you are just working with your own data call the API using your personal API key (available towards the bottom of the settings page) and basic authentication.\n\n## Heading link Uploading completed activities\n\nThis is done by POSTing multipart/form-data. Example using an access\\_token from OAuth (ACTIVITY:WRITE scope is required):\n\n```lang-auto\n$ curl -F file=@i55610271.fit \\\n    'https://intervals.icu/api/v1/athlete/0/activities?name=Foo&description=Bar' \\\n    -H 'Authorization: Bearer d842c1fc25f241e5ae440d09756448a9'\n\n```\n\nSame example using a personal API key:\n\n```lang-auto\n$ curl -F file=@i55610271.fit \\\n    'https://intervals.icu/api/v1/athlete/0/activities?name=Foo&description=Bar' \\\n    -u API_KEY:6dzmsans11bsyifjxchr87oum\n\n```\n\nThe name and description URL parameters are optional. The file can be fit, tcx or gpx or a zip or gz of the same. There is also an optional external\\_id parameter which you can set to your own activity ID. You can configure an activity URL template for your application and Intervals.icu will use this and the external\\_id to link back to your application from the activity pages.\n\nNote that the athlete id in the path is ‘0’. This indicates that the athlete ID that the access\\_token or API key belongs to should be used.\n\n## Heading link Downloading planned workouts\n\nSee Downloading planned workouts from the API\n\n## Heading link Uploading planned workouts\n\nSee Uploading planned workouts to Intervals.icu\n\n## Heading link Updating wellness data\n\nPush weight, resting HR, HRV, steps etc. using the bulk wellness upload endpoint (WELLNESS:WRITE scope required):\n\n```lang-bash\ncurl -X PUT 'https://intervals.icu/api/v1/athlete/0/wellness-bulk' \\\n    -H 'Authorization: Bearer d842c1fc25f241e5ae440d09756448a9' \\\n    -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n    -d '[{\"id\":\"2024-11-20\",\"weight\": 69.1},{\"id\":\"2024-11-19\",\"weight\": 69.3}]'\n\n```\n\nEach object in the array must have an id (the ISO-8601 local date of the record) and whatever other fields you want to update. See the full docs for a list of possible fields. All units are metric.\n\n## Heading link Downloading wellness data\n\nCall the list wellness endpoint (WELLNESS:READ scope required):\n\n```lang-bash\ncurl 'https://intervals.icu/api/v1/athlete/0/wellness?oldest=2024-11-18&newest=2024-11-20' \\\n    -H 'Authorization: Bearer d842c1fc25f241e5ae440d09756448a9'\n\n```\n\n## Heading link Downloading completed activities\n\nCall the list activities endpoint (ACTIVITY:READ scope is required):\n\n```lang-bash\ncurl 'https://intervals.icu/api/v1/athlete/0/activities?oldest=2024-11-19&newest=2024-11-20' \\\n    -H 'Authorization: Bearer d842c1fc25f241e5ae440d09756448a9'\n\n```\n\nThis returns summary data for each activity. Example abridged response:\n\n```lang-auto\n[{\n  \"id\": \"i55751783\",\n  \"start_date_local\": \"2024-11-20T07:35:18\",\n  \"type\": \"Ride\",\n  ...\n  \"file_type\": \"fit\",\n  ...\n\n```\n\nTo download the original activity file (fit, gpx or tcx) gzip compressed:\n\n```lang-bash\ncurl 'https://intervals.icu/api/v1/activity/i55751783/file' \\\n    -H 'Authorization: Bearer d842c1fc25f241e5ae440d09756448a9' \\\n    > activity.fit.gz\n\n```\n\nTo download the Intervals.icu generated fit file (with edits to activity power etc. and laps matching the intervals):\n\n```lang-bash\ncurl 'https://intervals.icu/api/v1/activity/i55751783/fit-file' \\\n    -H 'Authorization: Bearer d842c1fc25f241e5ae440d09756448a9' \\\n    > activity.fit.gz\n\n```\n\nNote that this is always a fit file even if the original file was a gpx or tcx.\n\n## Heading link User Signup\n\nThe Intervals.icu signup form accepts query parameters to pre-populate the form with data you might already have:\n\n> https://intervals.icu/signup?email=foo&name=bar&ftp=280&max\\_hr=188&sex=M&weight=69.6\n\nWe are considering a paid white label option to allow new users to be created using the API.\n\n## Heading link Webhooks\n\nConfigure webhooks using the management page for your app. Look for your app in /settings and click “Manage App”.\n\nNote that activity webhooks are not delivered for Strava activities.\n\nThe CALENDAR\\_EVENT\\_UPDATED and CALENDAR\\_EVENT\\_DELETED webhooks are legacy. Please use the CALENDAR\\_UPDATED webhook instead.\n\nThe webhook POST payload includes a secret that you can use to verify that the webhook came from Intervals.icu.\n\n```lang-json\n{\n  \"secret\": \"ooKeodacie8I\",\n  \"events\": [\n    {\n      \"athlete_id\": \"...\",\n      \"type\": \"ACTIVITY_UPLOADED\",\n      \"timestamp\": \"2024-12-06T06:40:47.011+00:00\",\n      \"activity\": {...}\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n```\n\nSome webhooks (e.g. ACTIVITY\\_ANALYZED) are sent after a 60s delay so multiple events for the same activity can be consolidated into one webhook.\n\nYou need to store the Intervals.icu athlete\\_id obtained via OAuth flow so you can map the webhook back to the athlete in your system.\n\nCALENDAR\\_UPDATED webhooks include oauth\\_client\\_id (that created the event if any) and external\\_id (ID supplied when the event was created, if any). You can use this to only look at events created by your app (oauth\\_client\\_id matches your client ID) and quickly update them using the external\\_id.\n\n```lang-auto\n{\n  \"secret\": \"...\",\n  \"events\": [\n    {\n      \"athlete_id\": \"2049151\",\n      \"type\": \"CALENDAR_UPDATED\",\n      \"timestamp\": \"2024-12-18T10:22:16.427+00:00\",\n      \"events\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": 48566307,\n          \"start_date_local\": \"2024-12-20T00:00:00\",\n          \"icu_training_load\": 118,\n          \"type\": \"Ride\",\n          ...\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": 48566308,\n          \"start_date_local\": \"2024-12-21T00:00:00\",\n          \"icu_training_load\": 82,\n          ...\n        }\n      ],\n      \"deleted_events\": []\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n```\n\nThe SPORT\\_SETTINGS\\_UPDATED webhook is fired when an athletes FTP, zones etc. are changed."}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_7ZqNvRBn65KEdpcY7vrLkvmE","content":"The returned content is the main text extracted from the page. If you use it in your answer, cite this page as a markdown link, e.g. [title](url).\n\nIntervals.icu uses OAuth2 for authentication to the API. OAuth allows external applications to request authorization to access an Intervals.icu user’s data. It allows users to grant and revoke API access on a per-application basis and keeps user authentication details safe.\n\n## Heading link Creating An Application\n\nFill in the application form here: https://intervals.icu/oauth/apply\n\nYou need to be logged in as the Intervals.icu athlete that will own the app. This athlete will have access to the management page to edit the app, setup redirect URI’s, webhooks and other things.\n\nYour app will show up on the /settings/apps page (only for you as the owner) and you can click “Manage App” to retrieve your client\\_id and secret, change redirect URL’s, configure webhooks and so on.\n\n\n![image1](https://kimi-web-img.kimi.ai/prod-data/online-image/search-upload/cb935eaa9a1b9e784347f5a9486fe24a.png)\n\nThe app will have status “Pending” until it is approved. **Please note that you will not be able to do the OAuth flow until it is approved**. You can upload a logo, get the client ID and secret and so on.\n\nOnce it has been approved, the pending tag will disappear. You will receive a system notification when this happens (delivered by email and in the Intervals.icu app).\n\nNote that it will not be visible to other users in /settings/apps, but you can send anyone you like to the OAuth consent page and begin integration.\n\n\n![image2](https://kimi-web-img.kimi.ai/prod-data/online-image/search-upload/ef7703e10049bf07ae1b507e4796aacc.png)\n\nWhen you have completed your integration and tested properly, contact support@intervals.icu to have it listed in the public app directory. Please include a link to the management page in the email.\n\n## Heading link Requesting Authorization To Access Intervals.icu Data For A User\n\nSend the user to:\n\n```lang-auto\nhttps://intervals.icu/oauth/authorize?client_id=<your client id>\n    &redirect_uri=<your redirect uri>\n    &scope=<required scopes>\n    &state=<optional data>\n\n```\n\nIntervals.icu will ask the user to login and display a confirmation dialog with options to choose which\n\nscopes to grant the application. If the user confirms then they are redirected to the redirect\\_uri with an\n\nauthorization code and the optional state parameter:\n\n```lang-auto\n<your redirect uri>?code=3983ed415f66413c890ca48b7cce59e4&state=...\n\n```\n\nIf they decline:\n\n```lang-auto\n<your redirect uri>?error=access_denied\n\n```\n\nYour server needs to exchange the code for an access token within 2 minutes by POSTing form data including your client\\_id and client\\_secret:\n\n```lang-auto\ncurl -X POST https://intervals.icu/api/oauth/token \\\n    -d client_id=... \\\n    -d client_secret=... \\\n    -d code=3983ed415f66413c890ca48b7cce59e4\n\n```\n\nIf all goes well Intervals.icu will respond with an access token, granted scopes and the id and name of the athlete:\n\n```lang-auto\n{\n    \"token_type\": \"Bearer\",\n    \"access_token\": \"d842c1fc25f241e5ae440d09756448a9\",\n    \"scope\": \"ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:WRITE\",\n    \"athlete\": {\n        \"id\": \"2049151\",\n        \"name\": \"David (intervals.icu)\"\n    }\n}\n\n```\n\nTo call the API use “Authorization: Bearer d842c1fc25f241e5ae440d09756448a9” header.\n\nNote that you can use “0” for the athlete id for endpoints that accept an athlete id in the path. This will use the athlete for the bearer token used to make the call.\n\n### Heading link PKCE (optional)\n\nPKCE is supported to protect the authorization code from interception. Generate a random `code_verifier` (43-128 chars of `A-Z a-z 0-9 - . _ ~`) and add its challenge to the authorize URL (only `S256` is supported):\n\n```\n    &code_challenge=<BASE64URL(SHA256(code_verifier)) without padding>\n    &code_challenge_method=S256\n\n```\n\nThen include `-d code_verifier=...` when exchanging the code. If a challenge was sent, the verifier is required, and a verifier is rejected if no challenge was sent. The client\\_secret is still required unless your app is a public client.\n\nOnce every version of your app uses PKCE, tick “Require PKCE” on your app’s settings page. Authorizations without a code\\_challenge are then rejected, and so is exchanging a code without a code\\_verifier, even with the client\\_secret.\n\n### Heading link Public clients (SPA, mobile and desktop apps)\n\nApps that cannot keep a client\\_secret confidential can be flagged as public clients on the OAuth app management page. Public clients that use PKCE can omit client\\_secret when exchanging the code. Without PKCE the client\\_secret is still required (this is supported so existing apps can migrate, please switch to PKCE). The automatic http://localhost redirect exception does not apply to public clients, so register the exact redirect URIs you use, including any localhost ones. The port of a registered http://localhost or http://127.0.0.1 redirect is ignored, so native apps can listen on any free port:\n\n```\ncurl -X POST https://intervals.icu/api/oauth/token \\\n    -d client_id=...\n    -d code=3983ed415f66413c890ca48b7cce59e4\n    -d code_verifier=...\n\n```\n\n## Heading link Scopes\n\nScopes are as follows:\n\n- ACTIVITY: Completed rides, runs etc.\n- WELLNESS: Weight, resting HR etc.\n- CALENDAR: Planned workouts\n- CHATS: Chats, groups and messages\n- LIBRARY: Workout library\n- SETTINGS: Athlete settings\n\nFor each scope specify READ or WRITE (to update, implies READ access) and use commas to separate multiple scopes. Example:\n\n```lang-auto\nACTIVITY:READ,WELLNESS:WRITE\n\n```\n\nRequests read access to activities and read and write access to wellness data.\n\n## Heading link Revoking An Access Token\n\nWhen a user disconnects Intervals.icu in your app or deletes their data on your side, revoke the access token:\n\n```lang-auto\ncurl -X DELETE \"https://intervals.icu/api/v1/disconnect-app\" \\\n -H 'authorization: Bearer d842c1fc25f241e5ae440d09756448a9'\n\n```\n\nThis will stop webhook delivery for the athlete.\n\n## Heading link Your Own Data\n\nNote that you don’t need to do all this if you just want access to your own data. Use your API key to do that.\n\n## Heading link API Endpoints"}
{"role":"assistant","content":"Документация подтвердила важные факты. Теперь проверю README и саму строку SCOPES на скрытые символы — по логам именно добавление календарных scope сломало authorize-шаг.","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"tool_bGcr4kSSUG78OUXhjs0L7GVC","function":{"name":"Read","arguments":"{\"path\":\"README.md\"}"}},{"type":"function","id":"tool_4zTjM7naPft9kyvxtm5TTMPo","function":{"name":"Bash","arguments":"{\"command\":\"grep -n \\\"SCOPES\\\" config.py | cat -A; echo ---; sed -n '11p' config.py | xxd | head -20\",\"cwd\":\"/private/tmp/h-Gs7Fy2\"}"}}]}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_bGcr4kSSUG78OUXhjs0L7GVC","content":"1\t# tricoach\n2\t\n3\tBackend + single-page app for a small triathlon coaching practice. Coaches\n4\tplan the week; athletes see it and connect their Intervals.icu account so the\n5\tapp can read wellness data and push planned workouts to their calendar. The\n6\tathlete signs in to tricoach (token in `localStorage`, sent as\n7\t`Authorization: Bearer` by the SPA's fetch wrapper), then clicks\n8\t\"Connect Intervals.icu\", which runs the OAuth flow against Intervals.\n9\t\n10\t`server.py` is stdlib only (`python3 server.py`, port 8766) and keeps\n11\teverything in memory; the shape is the same as the Postgres tables in prod.\n12\tDev sign-in tokens: `tok-okafor` (default in the SPA) and `tok-rivera`.\n13\t`config.py` holds the OAuth client placeholders. `logs/` has what we captured\n14\twhile looking into the connection problems."}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_4zTjM7naPft9kyvxtm5TTMPo","content":"11:SCOPES = \"ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE\"$\n---\n00000000: 5343 4f50 4553 203d 2022 4143 5449 5649  SCOPES = \"ACTIVI\n00000010: 5459 3a52 4541 442c 4143 5449 5649 5459  TY:READ,ACTIVITY\n00000020: 3a57 5249 5445 2c57 454c 4c4e 4553 533a  :WRITE,WELLNESS:\n00000030: 5245 4144 2c43 414c 454e 4441 523a 5245  READ,CALENDAR:RE\n00000040: 4144 2c43 414c 454e 4441 523a 5752 4954  AD,CALENDAR:WRIT\n00000050: 4522 0a                                  E\".\n"}
{"role":"assistant","content":"Строка SCOPES чистая. Проверю более поздние страницы треда про OAuth — там должен быть актуальный список scope и возможные ограничения.","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"tool_rzv5JaPF3JgkICeplHxiw8OO","function":{"name":"FetchURL","arguments":"{\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-oauth-support/2759?page=2\"}"}}]}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_rzv5JaPF3JgkICeplHxiw8OO","content":"The returned content is the main text extracted from the page. If you use it in your answer, cite this page as a markdown link, e.g. [title](url).\n\n## post by pmcarlos on Aug 31, 2022\n\nThanks for your response, I’ll update my app accordingly then\n\n## post by david on Sep 2, 2022\n\nIt is as app4g says. I am planning to support multiple access tokens per app soon. That was an oversight on my part.\n\n1 year later\n\n\n## post by Leonid\\_Kholkine on Sep 21, 2023\n\nComing back to this, is multi access token already supported?\n\nThanks!\n\n10 days later\n\n\n## post by david on Oct 1, 2023\n\nI just implemented that. There can be many access tokens for an athlete linked to an app, once for each time they authorise it. The most recent scopes apply to all access tokens.\n\n1 month later\n\n\n## post by Leonid\\_Kholkine on Nov 7, 2023\n\nThanks! One more question, is there also a scope for managing my athletes? The use case it’s that coaches will be connecting to intervals.\n\nEDIT: Found it in Swagger, there is a ATHLETES scope, but still doesn’t seem to work.\n\nEDIT2: It seems accessing /athletes seems to work with my own API key but not through the bearer token where I get 403.\n\n## post by david on Nov 8, 2023\n\nCurrently oauth tokens grant access to the authorising athlete’s data but not to people they follow or coach. This is by design so someone who follows you can’t auth a 3rd party app which then gains access to your data. I think you need to get each athlete to auth your app and then use the correct token depending on the athlete.\n\nWill this work?\n\n## post by Leonid\\_Kholkine on Nov 8, 2023\n\nThe only (specific) issue to us, it’s that we work with coaches and use there data. Unfortunatly our whole data platform is built around the idea of 1 connection → multiple athletes. This was following the same logic as TrainingPeaks basically, where the coached athletes are also available through the API.\n\n7 months later\n\n\n## post by Aart\\_Goossens on Jun 12, 2024\n\nIs there a way to have intervals.icu push new activities for a user to an application?\n\nAlternatively, I could regularly poll the API for new activities. Is there a rate limit in place that would limit this solution?\n\nThe rate limiting question is also relevant for the backfill scenario (where users first authorize the application and where the applications needs to process historical activities). Are there any limitations on doing that?\n\n## post by david on Jun 13, 2024\n\n\nThere are are rate limits but they are very generous and you aren’t likely to get a 429. They are there mostly to protect the server app from bugs in the Intervals.icu client\n\n![image1](https://kimi-web-img.kimi.ai/prod-data/online-image/search-upload/39a7d733bfd9e00ee3fd31c2b41c7238.png)\n\nSo backfill shouldn’t be a problem.\n\nThere is some undocumented support for webhooks. If you send me one or two web hook URLs (e.g. one dev one prod). I will set that up for you.\n\n## post by Aart\\_Goossens on Jun 13, 2024\n\nThanks for the reply. I’ll reach out to you as soon as I’m ready for integration!\n\n6 months later\n\n\n## post by david on Dec 6, 2024\n\nThere is now a management page for each OAuth application. You can view your client\\_id and secret, change redirect URL’s, enable webhooks and so on. Apps that you own on the /settings page get a “Manage App” button:\n\n\n![image2](https://kimi-web-img.kimi.ai/prod-data/online-image/search-upload/ef7703e10049bf07ae1b507e4796aacc.png)\n\n![image3](https://kimi-web-img.kimi.ai/prod-data/online-image/search-upload/f5938d5f8d27d450a374fc2a82cec171.png)\n\n2 months later\n\n\n## post by John\\_Peters\\_endura.f on Feb 4, 2025\n\nHi David - just noticed this. Does this mean you have webhooks in intervals now as well as the REST API?\n\nCheers\n\nJohn\n\n## post by david on Feb 4, 2025\n\nYes that is correct. You can just tick the boxes for the ones you want to receive.\n\n## post by John\\_Peters\\_endura.f on Feb 4, 2025\n\nJust trying to test this using the wellness updated endpoint. Is it a POST method required at my end to receive the data? I don’t seem to be getting anything coming through at the moment when I change my wellness data\n\n## post by david on Feb 4, 2025\n\nYes it is a POST. I forgot to mention that in the doc and have just added it.\n\n## post by John\\_Peters\\_endura.f on Feb 4, 2025\n\nThanks. Is there an easy way of figuring out what I’m doing wrong. My endpoints work testing in postman when I send a json file (I’m just dumping it in a DB for the moment), but I’m not getting anything through from Intervals when I change my calendar or wellness data.\n\n## post by david on Feb 4, 2025\n\nIts giving a 404:\n\n> 2025-02-04 14:12:29.248 DEBUG 1 — \\[ok-publisher-12\\] i.i.service.WebhookPublisherService : Error posting webhook i68403:WELLNESS\\_UPDATED:2025-02-04 xxx/, retry(4): icu.intervals.util.HttpStatusCodeException: Got 404 {“error”:“404 - Resource Not Found”}\n\nThat xxx is your webhook URL. Realised I shouldn’t post that here!\n\n3 months later\n\n\n## post by Aart\\_Goossens on Apr 25, 2025\n\nIt looks like wildcard redirect uris for applications are not working properly and result in an “Invalid redirect\\_uri” error. The hint for “ http://localhost/\\*” on the application management page suggests that wildcard redirect uris are supported.\n\nIn my case, “ https://app.sweatstack.no/\\*” didn’t work, but providing the full redirect uri did.\n\nAlthough some (most?) cases can be handled with the `state` query parameter, it would be nice to support wildcard redirect uris.\n\n## post by david on Apr 28, 2025\n\nI see. Yes wildcards are not supported. I will see what I can do about that.\n\n14 days later\n\n\n## post by Lady\\_Jesikat on May 13, 2025\n\nAlso, for localhost URIs, can the port number be ignored?"}
