{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_lpm6jTDwk39InK1SmeaqzcPw","content":"Title: CAMARA Security and Interoperability Profile\nSite: Github\nURL: https://github.com/camaraproject/IdentityAndConsentManagement/blob/main/documentation/CAMARA-Security-Interoperability.md\nSnippet: ... Authorization Server returns an invalid_request error code. For CIBA please ... invalid_scope, The requested scope is either invalid, unknown, or ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: vscode/src/vs/base/common/oauth.ts at main\nSite: Github\nURL: https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/blob/main/src/vs/base/common/oauth.ts\nSnippet: / export const enum AuthorizationErrorType { InvalidRequest = 'invalid_request ... invalid_scope' } /* * Device authorization grant specific error codes as ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: OAuth fails with \"Invalid authorization request\" at mcp.notion.com/authorize\nSite: Github\nDate: 2026-08-05\nURL: https://github.com/anthropics/claude-ai-mcp/issues/776\nSnippet: Issue details ``` MCP server URL or name: mcp.notion.com How are you connecting: Both from the MCP server directory and as a custom connector (https://mcp.notion.com/mcp) Where does the issue occur: In the authorization screen When did you last reproduce this: 2026-08-05, ~12:40 JST Browser and OS: Chrome, macOS (Claude Desktop + claude.ai web) Description: The Notion connector disappeared from my connected connectors. When I try to reconnect, the OAuth flow fails immediately at `https://mcp.not\n\n---\n\nTitle: Trakt OAuth cannot complete: Trakt's new authorize endpoint injects PKCE, auth.servarr.com exchange fails with \"Received oauth token was invalid.\"\nSite: Github\nDate: 2026-08-01\nURL: https://github.com/Radarr/Radarr/issues/11580\nSnippet: Current Behavior PKCE requires whoever redeems the authorization code to present the matching `code_verifier`. The legacy flow never generated one, so `auth.servarr.com` has nothing to send at the token-exchange step, and the exchange fails. The user-visible string comes from that endpoint: ```notranslate $ curl -s -w '\\n[%{http_code}]\\n' 'https://auth.servarr.com/v1/trakt/auth?code=dummycode&state=http%3A%2F%2Flocalhost%3A7878%2Foauth.html' Received oauth token was invalid. [400] ``` This also \n\n---\n\nTitle: Getting an error as \"Unable to authorize access because the client configuration is invalid: invalid_request\" while running OAuth Process | Adobe Sign\nSite: Adobe Help Center\nDate: 2021-04-27\nURL: https://helpx.adobe.com/sign/kb/unable-to-authorize-access-because-the-client-configuration-is-invalid-invalid-request-while-running-oauth-process.html\nSnippet: While running OAuth process to generate Access tokens, an error is encountered as \"Unable to authorize access because the client configuration is invalid: invalid_request\" in API. Environment OAuth Scope Documentation: https://secure.na1.echosign.com/public/oauthDemo Resolution While running OAuth Process, make sure to follow below points: 1. Correct Client ID and Redirect URI is specified. 2. Scopes provided in Authorization URL should match exactly with the scopes provided in Adobe Sign applic\n\n---\n\nTitle: oidc package - github.com/zitadel/oidc/v2/pkg/oidc\nSite: Go Packages\nDate: 2024-08-27\nURL: https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/zitadel/oidc/v2/pkg/oidc\nSnippet: const ( InvalidRequest errorType = \"invalid_request\" InvalidScope errorType = \"invalid_scope\" InvalidClient errorType = \"invalid_client ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: eBay OAuth Authorize Grant Flow Invalid Parameters\nSite: Stack Overflow\nDate: 2023-04-12\nURL: https://stackoverflow.com/questions/76000323/ebay-oauth-authorize-grant-flow-invalid-parameters\nSnippet: I'm using the ebay-oauth-java-client to get an authorization url, however, this seems to not be working and complaining Error message: ``` {\"error_id\":\"invalid_request\",\"error_description\":\"Input request parameters are invalid.\",\"http_status_code\":400} ``` auth url with client secret added to end: ``` https://auth.sandbox.ebay.com/oauth2/authorize?client_id=blabla-blabla-blabla-blabla-blabla&response_type=code&redirect_uri=http://localhost:8080/callback&scope=https://api.ebay.com/oauth/api_scope\n\n---\n\nTitle: Error-\"Unable to authorize access because the client configuration is invalid: invalid_request\". | Community\nSite: Adobe Support Community\nDate: 2024-03-27\nURL: https://community.adobe.com/questions-35/error-unable-to-authorize-access-because-the-client-configuration-is-invalid-invalid-request-14611\nSnippet: I'm trying to integrate Adobe Sign into our application. I found a step-by-step manual to do this ( https://www.adobe.io/apis/documentcloud/sign/docs.html#!adobedocs/adobe-sign/master/gstarted.md). So, I created an Application and configured OAuth access for it. I configured my application to handle HTTPS requests. I created a request to get the access token according to the documentation, and used the appropriate Client ID and redirect URI, but I got an error message: \"Unable to authorize acces\n\n---\n\nTitle: @zoreal/oauth2-js 0.1.24 on npm\nSite: Libraries.io\nDate: 2026-09-12\nURL: https://libraries.io/npm/@zoreal%2Foauth2-js\nSnippet: invalid_scope, OAuthFlowError, A scope not on the asset's allowed list, or a Tier B scope from a public client. /pair, invalid_request, OAuthFlowError, Missing ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: OpenProject: config/locales/en.yml\nSite: Fossies\nURL: https://fossies.org/linux/openproject/config/locales/en.yml\nSnippet: \" 5039 invalid_request: > 5040 OAuth2 Authorization Server responded with 'invalid_request'. ... invalid_scope: \"You are not allowed to access the ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: Release Notes | FusionAuth Docs\nSite: FusionAuth\nDate: 2026-11-04\nURL: https://fusionauth.io/docs/release-notes\nSnippet: Instead, the error message Invalid_Request. Missing_tenant_id is ... Previously, the request responded with an invalid_scope OAuth error. #2590.\n\nWhen you rely on a result in your answer, cite it inline as a markdown link, e.g. [title](url)."}
